@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<section class="home">
    <p class="eyebrow">Moser.RagAi</p>
    <h1>Intranet policy RAG</h1>
    <p>
        A policy file becomes one searchable row: the original text plus a point in meaning-space.
        A question lands near similar points; the model reads those texts, not the numbers.
    </p>
    <ol class="home-steps">
        <li class="step step-ingest">
            <p><strong>Ingest</strong> — walk one real file, then look at the index it creates.</p>
            <div id="ingest-graph">
                <div class="ig-toolbar">
                    <button type="button" class="ig-btn" data-ig="back" aria-label="Previous step">◀</button>
                    <button type="button" class="ig-btn primary" data-ig="next">Next</button>
                    <button type="button" class="ig-btn" data-ig="play">Play through</button>
                    <button type="button" class="ig-btn" data-ig="burst">Show whole seed</button>
                </div>
                <ol class="ig-rail" data-ig="rail"></ol>
                <article class="ig-teach" data-ig="teach">
                    <div class="ig-teach-kicker" data-ig="teachKick"></div>
                    <h3 data-ig="teachTitle"></h3>
                    <p class="ig-teach-why" data-ig="teachWhy"></p>
                    <div class="ig-teach-pair">
                        <div><span>Still true</span><p data-ig="teachSame"></p></div>
                        <div class="ig-new"><span>What changed</span><p data-ig="teachChange"></p></div>
                    </div>
                    <pre class="ig-doc" data-ig="teachDoc"></pre>
                    <div class="ig-meter" data-ig="teachMeter" hidden><i></i><b data-ig="teachMeterLbl"></b></div>
                    <div class="ig-vecbars" data-ig="teachVec" hidden></div>
                </article>
                <div class="ig-card">
                    <div class="ig-tiers"><span>Disk</span><span>Window</span><span>Coordinates</span><span>Shelf</span></div>
                    <div class="ig-scroll">
                        <div class="ig-board" data-ig="graph">
                            <svg class="ig-edges" data-ig="edges"></svg>
                            <div class="ig-cols" data-ig="cols"></div>
                            <div class="ig-flow" data-ig="flow"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ig-index">
                    <div class="ig-index-head">
                        <h3>The shelf</h3>
                        <p>
                            Search compares <b>where</b> rows sit. The model later reads <b>what they say</b>.
                            Clusters are a 2D sketch of 768-d space — same idea as a globe drawn on paper.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ig-probes">
                        <span class="ig-lens-label">Ask the map</span>
                        <button type="button" class="ig-btn" data-probe="expense">Need a receipt over $25?</button>
                        <button type="button" class="ig-btn" data-probe="gift">Cash gift from a supplier?</button>
                        <button type="button" class="ig-btn" data-probe="pto">How many PTO days?</button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ig-index-split">
                        <div class="ig-table-wrap">
                            <table class="ig-table">
                                <thead>
                                    <tr>
                                        <th>Id</th>
                                        <th>Text (model)</th>
                                        <th>Point (search)</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody data-ig="table"></tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                        <div class="ig-space-wrap">
                            <svg class="ig-space" data-ig="space" viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none"></svg>
                            <div class="ig-space-cap">Labeled neighborhoods · a question is a new point</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ig-ground" data-ig="ground">
                        <div class="ig-ground-kicker">What the model would read</div>
                        <p data-ig="groundBody">Finish the walk (or show the seed), then ask the map. Nearby texts — not vectors — go into the prompt.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li class="step step-retrieve">
            <p><strong>Retrieve</strong> — embed the question, find nearby points, keep chunks that also share words.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step step-generate">
            <p><strong>Generate</strong> — the model writes from those texts; C# Policy can still Deny.</p>
        </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="sr-only">
        Walk one policy file: it is text on disk, measured against a 640-token window and kept as one chunk,
        given 768-d coordinates without replacing the text, then stored as a row. Search finds nearby rows; the model reads their text.
    </p>
    <p>
        <a href="/assistant/ask">Ask</a>
        · <a href="/assistant/status">Live index</a>
        · <a href="/legend">How RAG works here</a>
    </p>
</section>
